# 低频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List03核心词汇

{{benevolent}}{/bɪˈnevələnt/}{仁慈的；慈善的}{The benevolent organization provides shelter for the homeless.}}
{{bestow}}{/bɪˈstəʊ/}{授予；赐予}{The university bestowed an honorary degree on the scientist.}}
{{betrayal}}{/bɪˈtreɪəl/}{背叛；出卖}{The betrayal of trust is difficult to forgive.}}
{{beverage}}{/ˈbevərɪdʒ/}{饮料}{Hot beverages are complimentary for hotel guests.}}
{{bizarre}}{/bɪˈzɑːr/}{奇异的；怪异的}{The bizarre incident attracted media attention.}}
{{blast}}{/blɑːst/}{爆炸；一阵}{A blast of wind knocked over the fence.}}
{{blaze}}{/bleɪz/}{火焰；熊熊燃烧}{The blaze spread rapidly through the dry forest.}}
{{blend}}{/blend/}{混合；融合}{The sauce is a blend of herbs and spices.}}
{{bliss}}{/blɪs/}{极乐；幸福}{The quiet countryside was pure bliss after the city noise.}}
{{blunt}}{/blʌnt/}{钝的；直言不讳的}{His blunt assessment of the situation was refreshing.}}
{{blur}}{/blɜːr/}{模糊；使模糊}{The boundary between work and home has blurred.}}
{{bold}}{/bəʊld/}{大胆的；醒目的}{The company made a bold move into the Asian market.}}
{{bond}}{/bɒnd/}{纽带；债券}{Shared experiences create strong bonds between people.}}
{{bonus}}{/ˈbəʊnəs/}{奖金；红利}{Employees received a performance bonus at year-end.}}
{{boycott}}{/ˈbɔɪkɒt/}{抵制；联合抵制}{Consumers organized a boycott of the brand's products.}}
{{brace}}{/breɪs/}{支架；支撑}{The city braced itself for the approaching storm.}}
{{brand}}{/brænd/}{品牌；商标}{The brand is synonymous with quality and reliability.}}
{{breakthrough}}{/ˈbreɪkθruː/}{突破；重大进展}{The new drug represents a breakthrough in cancer treatment.}}
{{breed}}{/briːd/}{品种；繁殖}{This breed of sheep is prized for its fine wool.}}
{{brink}}{/brɪŋk/}{边缘；濒临}{The species is on the brink of extinction.}}
{{brittle}}{/ˈbrɪtl/}{易碎的；脆弱的}{The economy remains brittle despite recent growth.}}
{{browse}}{/braʊz/}{浏览；吃草}{She browsed the bookstore for over an hour.}}
{{brutal}}{/ˈbruːtl/}{残忍的；严酷的}{The brutal competition in the industry drives innovation.}}
{{bubble}}{/ˈbʌbl/}{气泡；泡沫}{The housing bubble burst in 2008, triggering a recession.}}
{{bullet}}{/ˈbʊlɪt/}{子弹；弹头}{The report was a bullet point summary of the findings.}}
{{bulletin}}{/ˈbʊlɪtɪn/}{公告；简报}{The school issued a bulletin about the schedule change.}}
{{bureau}}{/ˈbjʊərəʊ/}{局；办事处}{The federal bureau investigates violations of the law.}}
{{bypass}}{/ˈbaɪpɑːs/}{绕过；旁路}{The new highway bypasses the congested city center.}}
{{cabin}}{/ˈkæbɪn/}{小屋；机舱}{The passengers were instructed to remain in the cabin.}}
{{cable}}{/ˈkeɪbl/}{电缆；有线电视}{The company laid fiber optic cables across the region.}}
